==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*tunglą}}, cognate with {{cog|goh|*zungal}} (see there) and Old English {{m|ang|tungol}}. Further etymology unknown; Pokorny reconstructs a PIE root ''*dengh-'' "to shine" just from this Germanic word and a Baltic word for "to seem, to appear" (Lithuanian ''diñga'').

===Noun===
{{non-noun|n}}

# [[moon]]

====Derived terms====
* {{l|non|tunglskin}}

